{
 "slug": "test/frozen-peak-recalc",
 "about": "Frozen peaks: Re-analyze's re-detection, Peak Min's projection, and what a load, a live frame, a capture, Save and Redo do to a measurement's peaks and their per-peak state — each through the app's own path. Each case starts a fresh analyzer (threshold −40, Taps 1) and runs its 'steps': the shared steps of tooling/analyzer-steps; {\"load\": {...}} — a .guitartap document the runner writes and reads with the edition's own reader, then loads as the app does: 'type' (the saved measurement type), 'spectrum' (the frozen spectrum, as a peaks.json spectrum spec; absent: none saved), 'peaks' ([hz, dB] — the saved peaks), and optionally 'selected' (hz), 'userModified', 'overrides' (hz → name), 'offsets' (hz → [x, y], a dragged label's position) and 'tapEntries' ({'peaks', 'selected'}); {\"loadFixture\": file} (a fixture every edition carries, loaded as the app loads a file); {\"reanalyze\": true}; {\"toggleSelection\": hz}; {\"nameMode\": {\"at\": hz, \"label\": s}}; {\"dragLabel\": {\"at\": hz, \"to\": [x, y]}}; {\"liveFrame\": spec} (a frame from the running engine); {\"save\": true}; {\"loadSaved\": true} (the last saved measurement, loaded); {\"mark\": true} (records the peak ids, the selected ids and the per-tap entries); {\"check\": {...}}. A peak is named by its frequency: the peak within 1 Hz of it (a dragged label, a name or a selection is resolved to its peak's frequency the same way; one on no peak fails the check). Fields: 'peaks' (the measurement's peaks, ascending), 'shown' (those above Peak Min), 'selected' (the selected peaks), 'overrides' and 'offsets' (the whole map, by frequency), 'labels' (hz → the label the analyzer gives that peak — the name the results show), 'modes' (each peak's classified mode, the whole map), 'tapEntries' (each entry's peaks and selected peaks), 'idsAsMarked' / 'selectedIdsAsMarked' / 'tapEntriesAsMarked' (unchanged since the mark), 'idsAsLoaded' (the peak ids are the file's), 'canReanalyze', 'complete', 'phase' (Swift's raw value), 'fL' / 'fC' (the identified peak's frequency, null for none), 'materialPeaks' (the identified peaks), 'saved' (the last saved measurement: its 'peaks', and 'selectedAll'). 'tapEntryModes': a tap entry's Air/Top/Back, resolved from its 'peaks' ([hz, dB]) and 'selected' under 'guitarType' — mode → frequency. Retired: PR05, PR10, PR11 (guards no path reached, removed), PR26, PR27 (a carry-forward of a hand-made selection no path reached, removed), PR06, PR31. Expected values are Swift's.",
 "cases": [
  {
   "id": "PR01",
   "note": "Re-analyze detects the frozen spectrum's peak, and it is shown above Peak Min",
   "steps": [
    {
     "load": {
      "type": "Generic Guitar",
      "peaks": [],
      "spectrum": {
       "kind": "gaussians",
       "binCount": 601,
       "binSpacingHz": 1,
       "noiseFloor": -100,
       "peaks": [
        {
         "peakHz": 200,
         "peakDB": -20,
         "halfWidthHz": 7
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "setPeakMin": -60
    },
    {
     "reanalyze": true
    }
   ],
   "expect": {
    "peaks": [
     200
    ],
    "shown": [
     200
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "PR02",
   "note": "Peak Min hides a weak re-detected peak from the display; the measurement keeps it",
   "steps": [
    {
     "load": {
      "type": "Generic Guitar",
      "peaks": [],
      "spectrum": {
       "kind": "gaussians",
       "binCount": 601,
       "binSpacingHz": 1,
       "noiseFloor": -100,
       "peaks": [
        {
         "peakHz": 200,
         "peakDB": -50,
         "halfWidthHz": 7
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "setPeakMin": -60
    },
    {
     "reanalyze": true
    },
    {
     "check": {
      "shown": [
       200
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "setPeakMin": -40
    }
   ],
   "expect": {
    "shown": [],
    "peaks": [
     200
    ]
   }
  },
  {
